			"notes": "Open the animated guide with **?** in the Flux Gadget. The five lessons cover setup, linking machines, shared power, status readings and upgrades. Pause, replay or drag the timeline to revisit a step.\n\nCaptions and settings now have more room at large GUI scales. Long network names show their full text on hover, and list paging stays clear of nearby controls.\n\nFlux Pylons is available for Minecraft 1.20.1 on Forge and Fabric, and 1.21.1 on NeoForge, Forge and Fabric.\n\n| File | Minecraft | Loader | Java |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `flux-pylons-1.2.0.jar` | 1.21.1 | NeoForge 21.1.206+ | 21 |\n| `flux-pylons-forge-1.21.1-1.2.0.jar` | 1.21.1 | Forge 52.1.0+ | 21 |\n| `flux-pylons-fabric-1.21.1-1.2.0.jar` | 1.21.1 | Fabric Loader 0.16.14+ | 21 |\n| `flux-pylons-forge-1.20.1-1.2.0.jar` | 1.20.1 | Forge 47.4.10+ | 17 |\n| `flux-pylons-fabric-1.20.1-1.2.0.jar` | 1.20.1 | Fabric Loader 0.16.14+ | 17 |\n\nThe Fabric builds require [Fabric API](https://modrinth.com/mod/fabric-api) and [Forge Config API Port](https://modrinth.com/mod/forge-config-api-port). Team Reborn's Energy API is bundled.\n\n[Wiki](https://github.com/shikyo13/Flux-Pylons/tree/main/docs/wiki) · [Report a bug](https://github.com/shikyo13/Flux-Pylons/issues) · [Source branches](https://github.com/shikyo13/Flux-Pylons/branches)"
